        <p>The CLERK said he once, much oppcard to the use of the word pauper as Mr. Mitchell war, and be did not think Mr. Mitchell or any other member, of the Board lusd found him using it !Once he came into their service, nor had be on any occasion written it except when it ! was a statutory word. Mr. Mitchell required an explanation of the item 't paupers in hoepitala end ncboole." That referred to patrons who were charge- I able to the Board in institutions over which they had ! no control, such as certified homes. The descriptitn</p>
