        <p>, At Widnes on Tuesday, Coroner Brighouse inquiry touching the death of George Banner. ti eigt t. of 20, Grove-street, Widnes, who was foi no Satorday in a shed belonging to the Vine Company, Logsdaleornad, Widnes. On the morning of the 25th ult. deceased work appkr..otly in good health, end ot 9.30 hen by the foreman of Ott yard to the mineral a bring some oxide of zinc. Dr. Schofield, who madea post-mortem, said de died from poisoning, caused by carbon-monoxide, The jury returned a verdict of Dentist:Me tore tine, caused by the escape of monoxide gas, of the owners were Dot aware."</p>
