        <p>In the course of. general discussion, the view was expressed thst the slimmer Annual excursion should he considerably extended. Jenkins hoped that instead of on annual inspection Attended by .1,0 visitors there could be an Attendance of lit leant 200. (liohr, hoar and applausit.) This, it was believed, would stimulxte interest in the work of the camp. Perhaps it might lc possible to arrange such • tripe, connection with some place of worship.</p>
