        <p>This remaak was made to a reporter by Miss Annie Scat, IN, High Si, Prescot, near Liverpool. "My health failed when I was about 16," con- tinued Miss Seal, now 20 years of age. "My strength fell away, and I lost all my colour. In time 1 could scarcely drag myself about through trembling so with weakness.</p>
        <p>" ThisZeakness was followed by loss of appetite. I began to feel giddy after meals, and flab. knee affected my heart, causing great distress. My head ached so badly at times that I thought I should go erary. I got weaker and felt thoroughly exhausted ; all my joints became stiff and painful, and my nerves became dreadfully upset. For months I did not have one good night's rest. , . . . . . . _ . .</p>
        <p>"My feet and hands swelled, and I had very little use in my limbs. Ti, get upstairs was a breathless job, for each step made me moan with weakness and palpitation. Later, acute cramp seized me in the stomach. I also had a constant dragging pain across iny loins. One doctor said that I should always he an anemic, ailing woman. lint one day a lady advised me to try Dr. Williams' Pink Pills. I got a supple, and after I had taken the second lion my nerves got steady and my appetite returned. Gradually, the swelling went from my feet and hands. . . .</p>
        <p>"As I continued taking Dr. Williams Pink Pills every trace of the headaches and backache left me, and I slept well at nights. Daily I improved. The colour came hack to my face; my cheeks and limbs grew plump, and new, rich blood filled my veins. Thanks alone to Dr. Williams' Pink Pills every trace of the Anemia left nie, and I was soon completely restored to. !mint." . . . . _</p>
