      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0049" n="art0049">
        <head>FUNERAL BANQUET IN PREHISTORIC ENOLAND.</head>
        <p>A FUNERAL BANQUET IN PREHISTORIC ENOLAND.</p>
        <p>It Is impossible to resist the f•scination of endeavouring to reconstruct • funeral bantpiet in the England of • century before the Christian /Ira from the description given by Mr. Arthur J. Evens of the extratirdinsry End at Locktoys, the residence of the Mte Mr. tiering. Mare are remains which point to an unsuspected cirilisation in those far-olf times. The purpose of Om oseeting is explained by the area. some of which still contain burned human bonee.—"Constry Life.-</p>
        <p>OPLNIN. COO M ARK ItT ROKNERA AM, SMALL 1101.1,V3M—Tbres years ago • aettler at Mira River, Ceps Renton. Nova Scotia, prepared • patch of ;ironed of 100 rq..rn feet and planted strawberrise. The two following years he incresaed the plot op to a trifle over se acre in sink Daring the summer of 1910, the grower eold 3.000d015, worth of strawberries born {hi, land, and 2,000d015. of this wee clear profit. The trait Irao disponed of in the ready market, of the Cape Breton colliery towns.</p>
