      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0052" n="art0052">
        <head>Warrington Win at Swinton.</head>
        <p>Warrington Win at Swinton.</p>
        <p>The Warrington team accomplished n good perform nose on Saturday at Swinton, when they heat the Blues on their own ground by one try to nil. The bonito side well weakened by the abaence of Fairhurat sad Davies in the beck division, while Warrington had only one absentee in Brooks, the half heck. Showery vorinther during the morning had made the ground in • shocking ' state, but at the tittle fur the kickoff there wag no rain hut • strong breeze front goal to goal. About 3,00; TeArna,:—.</p>
        <p>Swinton—Griffith., heck Gartrell, Valentine, Whar- ton, and Parker, three-quarter backs ; Oat ateiss and Dan Davies, half hacks ; Blears, Barnett, Nl'Veigh, Preston, !Wilt% and Smith, forwards. Warrington—Tilley. heck ; Unawortb, Dickenson, Taylor and Waywell, three-quarter bark. ; Creevey sad Lloyd, half backs • Johnston, Morsan, I homes, Shugare, Cheaters inWl Skelhorn, forwards. Referee, Mr. Hirst, Dewabitry. Swinton won the toss and aided by the wind, they soon raided the IVitrrington lino. Tilley defended well and a clever punt found touch near centre. Here I) ivies liroke awry, but gm, handling by the home 'centres rendered Warrington'a task navy. ltoes scrum- mage work followed hear the line, and Gartrell attempted to force his way over but waa grandly tackled by Unoworth. Then Johnston changed the scene with a fine dribble to centre. Here Warrington got posses- sion well, and Creevey started a passing movement on the right. Taylor kill Waywell got clear with exchange f;aasine and would certainly have scored hut for obatruction of Waywel I after plum- ing inside to Taylor. Swinton rime again and DM Davies Wan prominent in getting the ball awsy. trio Valentine failed badly in trying to double between the Warrington centres. Hard play in the Marrington half followed, and the defence of the Wirepuller. proved easily superior to the home attack up to the interval, when there F. no score.</p>
        <p>-Cent,</p>
        <p>Warrington seemed to been escullent prospects of victory eller the change of ends, but a surprise wet in store for them. The Swinton foreard• dribbled the length of the field after the kick-ofT awl one of the hottest attacks on the Warring- ton line followed. For ten minutes Swinton scrimmaged within three yards of tbe line trot got no In every time. Th• %Warrington men seemed blown, and nothing but the most desperate tackling by Wayweli, Tilley and Lloyd kept the Blues out. Once Parker got over ott wee knocked into touch in goal. Eventually Lloyd relieved with A short punt • hick Waywell followed to centre. Here the Warrinston roan seerneil to get their wicond wind and hest the Blues for possession. Creevey got away et centre and tricking the home halves made a beautiful opening for Dickenson end Unsworth. These two ran finely down the fold and beating the lull beck, Linitwprth •cored at the corner. Thorns, made • good attenTht st coal. From now to the end Warrington had the beet of matters,and finally yen out winners of a keen cantest by one try ..1 points), to oil. WIDNES FAIL AT SALFORD.</p>
        <p>This match, nt Weaste, attracted shoot 7,000 ptionle, and the game, although not of a scientific description, was keenly contested. The play in the enrolne ball was very even, and neither side could heat the defence, thongh Laws and Cook, for their teepee:ire sides, made good attempt.. In the second half some improvement weir shown by both terms, and early on Laws scored a good try for the visit.rs, l.,tt shortly afterwards John equalised for the home side. with a clever try. From now until the finish SliHord were by far the more •ggressire, and after Meal.); had given them the lead wink. brilliant try. May pit the lulls Imvond doubt by rimming the line. Result : —Salford, 3 tries (9 point.), Widnes I try (3 points). Teams : .9.lford—Larnbert, hack ; Coos, W. Thomas, kfealev. and Beene, three-quarter becli• Msv and John, half bank. : Ritchie, E. Thomas, Rees, Corm, Morton, and Warwick foreards. . .</p>
        <p>...R.iiines—Joner, hark Laws, Cisietetb, Tsylos gni, Swinton. threeopiarter bads Noon and Lally. Hilt bless S. Aspey, Cosgrove, Johnson, M'Carthy, Rigoy and Evans, forwards.</p>
        <p>"IRINGTON 4‘ A " V. So /STON 4."—This 70fItCh wss pinyed St Warrington on Saturday before 3,0*0 people. Flub and Lloyd were absentees front the Warrington ranks, end the visitors only broneht twelve men. A poor goo, was witnessed. neither side showing much cleverness. nsintith scored a try, and Mclntyre a goal, in esch half for Warrington. Jones, the Swinton full beck, dropped a capital 1051 for the visitors who were defeated by 10 points to 2 pointa.</p>
