      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0055" n="art0055">
        <head>RUNCORN Horse IX FLAME 3. EX4OOfRALLER”EFFRCTS A THRILLING</head>
        <p>RUNCORN Horse IX FLAME 3. EX4OOfRALLER”EFFRCTS A THRILLING</p>
        <p>RESCUE.</p>
        <p>An alarming fire occurred on Wednesdayat a dwelling house in GranYille-street. Runcorn. Airs. Jeckaon, the tenant, was at Warrington. and her daughter, Mrs. ' Pears.ll, was engaged in domestic work at the rear of the house, when neighbouts raised an alarm of fire. Mrs. Pearcill's child WAS ins bedroom, end the stair. case being found in Rimed, George Washburn, an old ROPV1•11 footballer, and a former member of the Black- burn Fire Brigale, elm. to the rescue. He procured a ladder, smashed the windows, and though four times driven hack by the smoke. he finally got the child out. Washburn collapsed immediately alter rescuing the infant. Two brigades got the flame. under, nut the interior of the house was gutted.</p>
