      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>Entertainment at Latchford.</head>
        <p>Entertainment at Latchford.</p>
        <p>A crowded salience witni .14.11 an entertainment on Monday evening in the Parish Room. Latchford, given by the Bolton Outahl t.chool scholar. depart- ment). Considering that the items were all performed without the s-i-istance of the " male" element,the pro- gramme was delighifully varied and interesting all through, and an appreciative umbels. exacted Loony encores. The programme consisted of choruses, songs hi character, and short sketches, and the viiutliful performers did ver7 well indeed in every cuse. The stir turn was Florence Watson's song " Imo an they do in England," her singing 1,.1 one so young being very sweet 55,1 true. Beryl Gilfurd in "'rim Chinese umbrella" provided one of the most pleasing items of the evening. The "Japanon fan song" made • pretty picture as did also the dance arid song "Jolly little .eishas." The song "Pliizzy-01-ni-01-cgee " was decidedly amusing,vrhile the sketch' new servant" by Annie Scott and Lilian Feutoli cauiteil much !laughter, the mistress's holitils skirt hiring in evidence. Miss Piave is noted for good enterminments and in this latest effort, assisted by Mi,.a I btrilfield and other ladies, full evidence was given of excellent training. Miss Bitchlield played the accompaniments in a finished manner.</p>
      </div>
