        <p>Mr Gilbert Greenell Buys Another Estate. The Lower Whitley evate, between Wm-sit:pion and Northwich, comprising (17, acres and including a fully licensed house, the property of Lieutenant- Colonel Sir Philip W. Chetwode, D.S.(J., was to have been offered for ~le by public auction on 11 ednesday at Warrington, tut on luesdny night it was announced by the auctioneers (Messrs. Manley and 'Sons, of Crewe), that Sir Gilbert tireenall, owner of the adjoining estates. had bought it privately. There are five large dairy farms, three villa ronitlenees, three I smell holdings, laid twelve cottages, while the public- bouse—the Chetwode Arms—in a well-known rood- side inn. The pile paid has not been made public, but the estimated value of the estate is about .4.:31,:a5e,</p>
