        <p>- -- -- A reguneulai tour (for officers and sergentel in connection with the 4th Baturlion Prince of Walee's Volunteers (South Lancashire Regiment) took piece on Saturds7 when the rendezvous was ilrappenhall, which was reached at about two o'cl,ck. the officers present were bout -Colonel J Fairclongh (corn- mauding the ith Battalion), Major B Fairqough, Captains G R Crosfield, A B Layton and HO Roberto, Lieutetiams Eger.on Fairclough, Eric Fairclough, Henshali, 11. McClure, M Woody, 0 L Whittle and F R Monk., and Captain and Adjutant i ColonelVerschoyle. commanding the brigade, was also preeent. The min, uvres were carried out with considerable skill, after which tea was served in the Large Room at Grappenhall, where Oolonel Verschoyle offered some criticism r.ri the work of the afternoon, and on the whole, it was favourable to all who had taken part in it,</p>
