        <head>DOMESTIC SERVANTS THEFTS.</head>
        <p>DOMESTIC SERVANTS THEFTS.</p>
        <p>At the Warrineton Police Court on ',ridgy (the Mayor in the chair) Esther Dollen, a domestic aaaaa nt, of Runcorn, WIN charged on remand with obtainifte by kirse pretences from Margaret leweon, certain goods to the val. of be. She was further charged with steal- ing from a dwelling hem., 7, Austin's-lane, a pftir of ladies' boots, and a gentleman. metal Albert watch and other articles value Its., the property of Margaret Lesson. A third charge wns ids° preferred against her, of stealing from a house In Disco-street, a blanket a sheet nod other articles, to the value of 13a Gil , the property of Mary Hurst. It was Rusted by the Chief Constable that on Monday, February 20th, prisoner went to the house of Margaret Lawson cod asked for •putmente, stating that ohs bad been recommended there. S' e ti ade a statement to the effect that her husband was the second officer on ft sailing boat and gave her name /Is Mrs. MlCribe. Alto, she had been there anion time she took the articles enumerated in the first and second charges and decamped. In the CABO of Mrs. Hurst it tens stated that prisoner went to her house wi, h it man named Raker, and when the left it was found that several article. had been stolen. .</p>
