        <p>• All Saints Mission Tea Party. The annoril ten party in connection with All Sainte Miion„ Hoyle-street. was held on Monday erasing and, as was anticipated, proved a great sitcom,. A large number of people ant down tons excellent tins, after which an admirable concert ose submitted. Mr. J. H. Smethurst presided and among those preetrat were the Revs. E. E. Peter. snit J. U. Wickes. The Chairman, in a short speech, remarked that • very good work was being married on at the mission, which was never lan more tlourialilng cecil- ties. Hr hoari wedtohnvd e i n htirretc,n. no i an. o‘res ct,rom.meeo di th ! om m b demands of the district. The artistes included Miss Wilkinson, who sweetly snag" Theawallows: and Mien Sudlow who gave good interpretation of Beautiful garden of roses." Mr. Shelley men at his beat in two of !terry Lauder's rongg and he a Iso finely rendered Thorn." Mr. J. E. Hannan contr Baited t nvo 1,0i08•nd Meagre. Walter Wright and A. Lendor graven comic. !net entitleale the upper ten and the lower five." Meaner John Morris's two comic songs brought the "b00..' down. The Bewsey Male Voice Choir inder the leader- ship of Mr. W. W right, charming rendered three or font glees onaccompsnied.lhecnt.cert concluded with, taros entitled 800. Nobs end Hobs," which ease taken part in by Meows. Walter Wright, Jaok Wright. P 'Wright, A Lander, Mites. L Helmet!, May Shaw and Lizzie Healey. The Rev J H Bank.. thanked the °Meese of ti. mission and the church workers for rallying round him in the way they bird done, and in conclusion be propcsed • cote of thanks to those nho hat helped to make the onteitainment a success. Our Lady a. Latchford. - - •</p>
