tion " end not • " fast " hut the proclamation hod eventually to: take the ancient form in order to make it • legal ' clotting day for banks and government office,. A hostion of Tea Drinkera—What becomes of the millions which the State dimmer's lathe *ape of old- er, pensions? It was said at fleet that the grocers, the cheap linen drapers, and the public homes, would benefit most by thin increased spending power on the rere:s of tho f oitgindiera*nr.thereirs onpoindioounbt7tErthteolahr;reer commeoption of lee, with the consequent inormse in price, is doe to this COMP, and there is, in many of the villages and towns, an air of greater prosperity moonset the email &amp;niters' shop.. Cpon the whole, there in reason to think thet lemur the pension money goes to the r ithlichomea then was antioipated. Tastes have changed since Queen Elisabeth and Mary Q.. of Sc,,?. deity thank their quart of etrong ale for breakfast and •Ithough there are medical men who do not regard it altogether with approval, we are more and more becoming • nation of tea drinkers. The Resit al of Fancy Needle, otk.—Art needlework Into a great extent taking the place of Bridge in the drawing-room. It in, at any rate, • more profitable, porsuit, seeing that it leads to some tangible reecho and there are few women who cannot If they like, pro- duce something useful in faocy work with cloth, silk end wool, hlaey are learning lace making, and it is Icing discovered that pillow-lace malting Is quite • pleasant way of npeochng leisure hours. A equal of tee lessons is rather costly, bet when Uoe art le acquired. It ism inexperalve hobby, and the Mos, If worked well, is both useful and valuable. The revival of afternoon needlework is largely due to the example net by the Queen, whole an expert onetllewomen, and make. • point of encouraging the donseetic arts lo every nonnitile eay. A Coin nation totem-10 hat shone., the Gaimboro' and Mammoth Napoleon are struggling for popular favour, but althotigh haling mi