        <p>VARI ETV COVART.—The Johnson Variety Concert Compel". •isited the school at Croft on Saturday night last. There was • good attendance. The concert wee composed of range, dancing and sleight of heed tricks. A feature of the concert was a local singing contest, the competitors being J Wood, T Crnston, F Collier, Fszakerly, W Rigby, P Collier, T Foster. The judges were the aildience,who gave their verdict in favour of Master P Collier and Mr J Wood. Thc evening proved very rationing and enjoyable. The Rey F I Waileson I said the promoters of the concert had given their rArriceis for the benellt of the Church funds and he heartily thenkeil them on behalf of the people of Croft for their kindness.</p>
        <p>CONI'ER I.—The Johnson's Variety Concert Company gave a successful concert in the Council school on Saturday evening. The Hector (Rev. H. I. Wadesoni said the promoter* of the concert had °Ser.d their service. that evening for the benefit o: the church funds and he most heartily thanked them on behalf of the parishioners and himself for their kindness. The entertainment consisted of songs, dancing, conjuring Sc., and tr,lll EI.Ch appreciated. An amusing incident took plane during theeveoing in the form of a Ringing competition confined to local tsiont and in whin'. seven competitots took part, vie. : Moser.. T. Croston, I). Paaskerley, H. Collier, W. Rigby, T. Foster, J. Wood and P. Collier (boy, After each competitor had wing the result NM left to the audience to decide as to their merits. The first five having been pot aside, the opinion of the audience we. taken on the remaining two, via.. J. Wood and time boy, P. Collier, and eventually the verdict aris equally divided, both sharing the winning honoura.</p>
