        <p>RUNCORN URBAN COCNCIL AND PLURAL VOTING.</p>
        <p>The mouthy meeting of the Runcorn Urban Diatrict Co toil was held on Wednenday, Mr. Carroll presiding. Mr. Hewitt (chairman of the Health Committee) maid that the annual report of the medical °dicer, now pre- sented, won highly natisfactory. The health of the town wan very good, and for the last three years the , death-rare was 139 par 1,000. 31r. (Buena oinked if any instructions were given to presiding °Ripens at the Urban Council elections with a view to stopping a person voting in two wards. If a roan voted in two wattle, menthe/9e tune penalty The Law Clerk replied that he would give npecial inntructions thin year to presiding °dicers. Toe only penalty was Lb* loss of the second vote. RUNCORN WOMEN'S LIBERAL ASSOCIATION. The ann.l meeting of thin orgsnination wan held at the Runcorn Liberal Chili on Wednesday. Mr..3l'Donald presiding. The hon. secretary (Mrs. .1. Holford reported that the association numbered 9.13 members, wah a breach at Halton of thirty members. While the general election wait on the ladies worked assiduounly and did capitel work in tracing removals, of which there were many on the eighteen months' old regieter. The associntion had aftlliated with the Womenk National sod the Lsncaahire and Cheshire Union of the Women', Liberal Asnociation. The total receipts were trol, and the expenditure £4l. The following officers were elected :—llon. president, MIA. J. F. L. Brunner ; president, 31 re. K. 11. Posnett ; hon. treasurer, Mrs. Sl'Doneld ; hon. necretary, Mr.. J Sol ford :tlmwncinl necretary, Mrs. M'lbrnald ; auditors, NIP.IS. Henry Wright and Alfred Dodd. Mrs. IL linker wan added to the list of •ice.orenidents.</p>
