        <head>RUNCORN BOARD OF OCARDIANS.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN BOARD OF OCARDIANS.</p>
        <p>Owing to an outbreak of scarlet fever among some of the inmates 1,1 the Dutton Workhouse, the fort- nightly meeting Board of Cluardians can held in the Runcorn Urban Council offic, instend of st Dutton Workhoone on Tuesday nfternoon. The good attendance testified to the enthusinnin of the member, of the Board in the dincharge of their dude. ; for many most have journeyed inconvenient distance, to attend the meeting. M r.. 1. Spruce presided. Th. caper. ',regent were : Mem/v.l.i. F. Ashton (clerk) W. R. de Prez, T. Cooke end J. Pennon (relieving officers). THE PENsions AND CoP.I.ENskTIoN. . . . . . .</p>
        <p>. ..... The Clerk nred-a-di.rcular letter from the Chester Union forwarding the following resolution and asking the Board to nuent to a similar one. That we, the Goardiaus of the poor of the Chester Union, In view of the fact that recipients of compensation under the Employerr Liability Acts are applying for poor law relief within a snits period of their receiving minor under the aforesaid Acts reapectfully petition hi. klajesty's Ministers to introduce logislatire at an early date enacting that all intern payable under the Employer. Liability Acts shall Inc vested in Ow Public Trustee or some other pension and paid to the recipiroita without deduction income eccerding to their require- ments" They asked that copier of the reeolution inn ',warded to Gin Prime Minister and to the local M.P.'s.</p>
        <p>........ Mr. L. F.. Linaker, jun., remarked that he thought that in Ulla district the compensation money waa always paid out piece-meal. Mr. Morria : I move that we support it. Mr. I.lbaker There will he no harm in that. Mr. Hallows seconded and this was unanimously agreed to.</p>
        <p>lioA It DINO-01:y OF CIIII.D.Itrt 1.1101,0111.</p>
        <p>Several recommendations the Boarding-Out Com- mittee in respect to what should be dotter with the Workhouse children were mentioned by the Clerk. They were as follows I, that the principle of the remov- ing of the children over three yeara of age from the Workhouse be adopted in this Union ; 3, that negotia- Gone ho opened for obtaining • suitable home or homes in wh'ch con he maintained thole children over whom the Guardians have not absolute control, and also f,,t the purpose of meriting therein those children over whom they have such control until such time as suit- able arrangements can be made for boarding them out or otherwise dealing with them as circumstance. will allow ; 3, that with respect to those children UV., whom the Guardians have absolute control arrangementn be made with institutions for wanting out within the Union ; (I, that tacit case. of boarded-oot children sent from the receiving home a payment of es. per week for maintenance and la per week for clothing be the standard rate of payment for each child.</p>
        <p>w•S resolv.-.1 that copies of the recomna•ndation be sent to sent to Peel member of the Board so as to give him time for the consideration of proposals which are it.horently drastic. The Ch.irman gave notioe that at the next meeting he worth! move that the report he adopted.</p>
        <p>EFFY.4 T OF PyNiION,I.ON POOR LAW FEW FM.</p>
