      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0137" n="art0137">
        <head>For the Cripples.</head>
        <p>For the Cripples.</p>
        <p>Sir,—May I presume upon yrtor courtesy to allow me to make appeal on behalf of the Cripples Guild M connection with the Bold-street Weeleyan Church. We have so many cripples who need help in the way of carringes. &amp;r. If any of your readers could let us have unused perambulatora, go-earth, snitches, or surgical appliances for cripples, they would be of exceeding service to some of the poor children who come under our care. I should be glad to hear from anyone who ran help us in this matter. Thanking you in anticipAion for your courtemy. I am yours truly, . WALTER SEED. .</p>
        <p>2. l'almyre-square. kVarrington.</p>
