        <head>SANKEY DRAINAGE.</head>
        <p>SANKEY DRAINAGE.</p>
        <p>—....... ..... lb. INSPECTOR reporied that he and the Medical officer had inspected the brook off Liverpool-road, Sankey. It was badly polluted with sewage, in. ffliby state and of a very objectionable character. Eight sewers were discharging into the brook. They sug- gested that to remedy the nuisance nine inch meow shoold be laid along the brook of 77:1 yards, eta. estimated cost of I:152.</p>
        <p>A report was read on the matter from the Sankey Parish Council, stating hat while the members were prepared to assist they acquiesced in any scheme whico would be in the interests of sanitary management they were so convinced that the suggested scheme was unnecesaary that the Council could not agree to it being carried out at the present time. The Council felt justi- fied in objecting to the scheme being carried out and suggested that a deputation be appointed to meet the Pariah Council on thivline of route. " " .</p>
        <p>Mr. FURNE., as chairnien of the Parish Conneil °mildewed that the report wee perfectly justille./ and thought that something should be done to minimise the offenaire character which the brook sometimes assumed. In the interests of the parish it would be better)! the scheme was carnal out.</p>
        <p>Ik. :11L'Illtal' &amp;eked if a scheme wan not submitted to the Parish Council 12 months ago. The INSPISCTuR said that was 50, and the expenditure sees &amp;wintered at £7O.</p>
        <p>The Meow.. tint Fit said the pr . scheme would not be. permanent or final one of .Sankey. It would be a part of a scheme which would have to follow. . .</p>
        <p>-It-was decided to eppoint the deputation to meet the Pariah Couocil ae auggeeted.</p>
