        <head>WORKINGMEN'S HOUSES Annual Meetings of Warrington Building Societies.</head>
        <p>WORKINGMEN'S HOUSES Annual Meetings of Warrington Building Societies.</p>
        <p>The enniod meeting .71' ill., Borough Werringt Os Incorporated Permanent Building Society P. held at the °thees of the manaser(Mr. Thomas Arthur Sutton), Legh-street.on Wednexiley evening. Mr. o.Holford pre- sided and there tries also present. MessroJohn Andrei. J T Saropeow 11 doughton (directors), J U Ceeppell T A Sutton (assessor end wirveyor ) end It Cook. The Directors in their thirty-sixth anneal report stated that the profit for the year after deducting working expense.. aninuoxed to Lirt 1. ii. The Directors ecommended the payment of a dividend at £4 nor rem per annum, free of Income Tax, which Ino .r.ke Lilt :Is. Id. mei ion...der to meet the deficit it wee proposed to transfer the sum of CU IS.. 4d. fore the reserve fund sccount. The co-operetion of emery member was wanted in order to obtain further a.m.-Pies and deposits. The oundwr of members on the hooks wits 36, of whore four were borrowers. Messrs G Holford, J Andrew., yam.. Grey, J Sampson. 11 Houghton tad IV Milner were re-elected directors and Mr J 6 Chappell. auditor.</p>
        <p>PritSIINENT HXF.FI r tIII.I,INf; Soctl• cr.</p>
        <p>There Win not a very large attendance et the 4Rh annual meeting of the Warrington Permanent Benefit Building Society held in Cairo-street schoolroom on Thursday evening. Mr W J Shaw, president of the society. occupied the chair. and amongst th:tse prw,ent were the following : Mtwara S W Delloar, C If Rib, err, T Inc., F 0 M,lling, T Partridge, It shackle- ton, F Tirnperley (directors, and W Woodcock auditor The report of the directors showed that the year bad been most wiccesssul one, and although witbdrawala through death and other causes had been largo, all chime had been promptly Paid. It was pleasing to report a marked increase in sultscription• and it mem- be.ship,and the Directors confidently looked forward to the co-operation of shareholders in introducing new memhers, as increase of business in thit direction would tend to inereee• the warning power of the wicket? which tam now in • thoroughly sound financial position. its Reserve Funds being moat to 15 per co it. of the share capital. The net profit on the year's working amminted to £lO9 15s 7:4, and the amount brought forward from lam vesr's account was £O2 la 11.1,m0k tag a total profit of £1:31 174 4d ior distribution, out of which the directors propose to pay a dividend of 11 per cent (free of income tax,, sad to carry the balance forward to next year'. account- The retiring directors were Messrs T face, T Partlidge. and R Shackleton who, being eligible, offered themmlves for re-election. Tb• Coo IRMAN remarked that the antallnem of the gathering ahowed the implicit confidence in which the wmiety wits regarded. 'I be balance sheet was one of the fineat that ham ever been produced since the eociety was inaugurated either by the present management or be the management which proceeded it. (Applause. luring the year they lied calla of • very wsvere char- acter made upon them—to the amount of £'.si—end those calla had been responded to by prnmpt payments. There had also been a great °inlay in niortnigee ~r thu beet character and then hoped to get good reterns through that business. Ile concludwl by moving the adoption of the accounts. Mr. Woo°, ock seconded, and remarked that during the year the tuernberthip had incremed from 2114 to Rhit, but they should not rent until they numbered VW. (Applause . The fonds of the society were used each- sive'? for making advances tm freehold and leasehold prenames. advance was made without n careful survey end a full valuation, end with • rear ,noble limit of reserve. The adage., were repaid by monthly instalments of principal and interest combined, and on terms that would appeal to all ; the tables running to 211 yearn, with. shorter period. if 'molted. The businese 1 an. not opeculative. se they di foot boy land oe houses, but only lent the money out on mortgage. , The retiring electors—Mtwara T Inc.. T Partridge. , end K Sheckleton—were unanimously re-electwl ea •Iso were the following fit:Jeers :—Tressurer, Mr Arpin&amp; Cook ; survevor, Mr William T. iss ; solicitor, Mr A J .wiliett ; maditors, Mr Edwin Bradshaw, V.C.A. ; Mr W .11 Woodcock, ApS.A.A. ; secretary, Mr A El Clive, C. Egvpustreet, Warrington. Mr. it St K prOpneert an honorarium, equal to the total amount of the fee f, attendance, be given to each director. The total sunk, he said, would not exceed E2O. .</p>
        <p>. FAIR secondsd and remarkad that ha dil not think that tbe society paid its directors adequataly. This coarse alma agreed to unanimously. On behalf of the Board, the CHAIRMAN briefy thanked the memfere.</p>
